# Curriculum Overview

## What is Insights from Data and AI about?
 
#### In this unit, students explore the foundational concepts of data science, focusing on developing and refining data questions to guide investigations and analysis. Through hands-on activities, they use spreadsheets for basic data analysis, explore ethical data practices, and learn how to communicate their findings using various visualization techniques. 

#### The unit begins with an introduction to data science concepts and progresses through lessons on data cleaning, visualization, and interpretation, concluding with a project that encourages students to tell a compelling data story using their newly acquired skills.


#### **This is the final unit in the six unit <a href='https://code.org/en-US/curriculum/artificial-intelligence-foundations' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>AI Foundations</a> semester 1 course. This professional learning module prepares you to teach it!**


## Student Learning Goals
